From 9d6a845d37c054ee2eb83a8401f54a2c6fbe4b55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:42:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: keep Snapdragon X on schedutil and uncapped outside
 power-saver

The performance governor held every core at full clock, idle ones
included: on a Zenbook A16 (X2 Elite) it drew 2W more at idle, and the
machine reset itself under load on battery. Omarchy gives the session's
processes a utilisation clamp floor that follows the profile instead,
which scored 42 in balanced and 45 in performance on Speedometer 3.1,
against 22 and 47 before. A 75% cap in balanced cost 6 of those points,
so only power-saver is capped now. Apple Silicon keeps the performance
governor in performance.
---
